A `Style` field reaches CSS, and an enum member reaches it spelled the way CSS
spells it: a multi-word member is the CSS keyword, not the identifier.

Two bugs met here. The IR-enum arm that restored `display:flex` wrote the
member verbatim, so every multi-word member came out camelCase --
`display:inlineBlock`, `justify-content:spaceBetween` -- turning a dropped
declaration into a wrong one. And seven declared fields had no prop-to-CSS
mapping at all and rendered as nothing, two of them added by the change that
needed them (docs/learn/tour.md styles with fontFamily, cursor and
borderLeft). internal/htmlutil's TestStyleFieldsAllReachCSS now enumerates
`Style`'s declared fields against the mapping so a new field cannot repeat it.

The looped span covers the lowered path, where the element is built by JS: a
style struct is not a value any DOM sink accepts, and passed through it
stringified to "[object Object]", so it has to be serialised to a declaration
list before it is written.

deny out/none/html/index.html `inlineBlock` -- the identifier spelling never reaches the stylesheet; only `display:inline-block` does
deny out/none/html/index.html `rowReverse` -- likewise for flex-direction, which CSS spells `row-reverse`
deny out/none/html/index.html `spaceBetween` -- likewise for justify-content, which CSS spells `space-between`
deny out/none/html/index.html `setAttribute\("style", \{` -- the style attribute is written as text, never as the struct itself

-- style.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:app"
import "sngl:platform/html"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

component main {
    var rows list<string> = ["a"]

    window {
        html.div(style={
            display = Display.inlineBlock,
            flexDirection = FlexDirection.rowReverse,
            justifyContent = Justification.spaceBetween,
            alignItems = Alignment.stretch,
            minWidth = 120,
            fontFamily = "Iosevka, monospace",
            borderBottom = "1px solid #ccc",
            borderLeft = "2px solid #000",
            borderCollapse = "collapse",
            borderStyle = BorderStyle.dashed,
            cursor = "pointer",
        })
        for var r = rows {
            html.span(textContent=r, style={display=Display.inlineBlock, cursor="pointer"})
        }
    }
}
-- out/none/html/index.html --
